WEBVTT

00:03.840 --> 00:07.140
In my life, I've killed 13 people.

00:11.330 --> 00:16.880
Compared to the average idiot,
I think I'm pretty strong.

00:19.740 --> 00:22.850
Killing is fun.

00:25.180 --> 00:29.940
The look on the face of
that posturing jarl's brat...

00:32.960 --> 00:34.610
That's how I know.

00:36.400 --> 00:40.970
This row of enemies in front of me...

00:50.780 --> 00:53.340
I'm scared! I'm scared, I'm scared...

00:53.340 --> 00:56.920
But damn it... they're enjoying this.

01:11.080 --> 01:13.080
Fuck!

01:17.640 --> 01:18.900
Gudmund!

01:22.560 --> 01:24.330
M-My legs...

01:26.630 --> 01:30.190
Ah, they're going to kill Badger.

01:30.470 --> 01:32.790
I don't believe it.

01:32.790 --> 01:36.190
How's he able to get so close
to the Jomsvikings?

01:47.520 --> 01:48.910
Boss?

01:49.220 --> 01:52.750
Fox, take Badger and fall back to the fort!

01:55.600 --> 01:58.550
All forces, retreat!

01:58.550 --> 02:00.970
Re—?! You can't be serious!

02:00.970 --> 02:02.550
I can still fight!

02:03.140 --> 02:06.260
Enough, Badger! Look around you!

02:06.740 --> 02:12.260
Damn it. Did all these men have to die for him
to know how much stronger the enemy is?

02:13.270 --> 02:16.020
Retreat!

02:16.020 --> 02:17.740
What? Retreat?

02:17.740 --> 02:19.650
All right!

02:21.650 --> 02:24.910
Don't bunch up! Spread out and flee!

02:25.240 --> 02:27.540
Wait for me! My legs...

02:29.260 --> 02:33.500
Retreat? I didn't order a retreat!

02:33.500 --> 02:38.290
Where's your honor?
And you call yourself Norse men!

02:38.290 --> 02:39.830
W-Wait up!

02:43.500 --> 02:45.390
I told you not to run.

02:46.000 --> 02:50.520
You think I'll forgive your debt after this?

02:53.700 --> 02:58.020
Debt? Either way,
you're finished, Mister Ketil.

03:00.170 --> 03:05.450
Do you understand what
it's like to be poor like us now?

03:06.510 --> 03:12.840
No matter how unfair it may be,
you shouldn't defy the king.

03:13.300 --> 03:17.710
It's the same reason we've
always listened to you!

03:18.990 --> 03:22.320
Might makes right, Mister Ketil.

03:22.950 --> 03:28.790
The world exists for people
stronger than you.

03:37.090 --> 03:37.980
They're here!

03:48.950 --> 03:50.500
What is it, Wulf?

03:49.450 --> 03:55.120
Pain

03:50.900 --> 03:52.540
Ah, Your Majesty.

03:53.300 --> 03:57.800
Someone who may have been Ketil
was just defeated by one of my men.

03:58.900 --> 04:03.050
How inept. My orders were to capture him.

04:03.480 --> 04:06.820
Yes, Your Majesty. I apologize.

04:06.820 --> 04:08.680
I'll go confirm what happened.

04:09.440 --> 04:12.710
The Jomsvikings are attacking
the backs of the fleeing soldiers.

04:12.710 --> 04:14.640
That goes against my orders as well.

04:15.000 --> 04:17.500
Tell Floki not to pursue them.

04:17.500 --> 04:18.370
Yes, Your Majesty.

04:30.300 --> 04:33.120
I'm not sure why,
but his guard captain left his side.

04:34.180 --> 04:35.830
This is my chance.

04:40.800 --> 04:43.140
Treat the bodies with care.

04:43.140 --> 04:44.880
We'll return them to their families—

04:50.190 --> 04:55.890
King Canute, your head is mine!

06:38.030 --> 06:40.220
Th-Thorgil!

06:40.220 --> 06:42.090
Where'd you come from?

06:44.140 --> 06:46.400
From Helheim.

06:50.750 --> 06:52.780
I'm surprised.

06:52.780 --> 06:55.740
I didn't think you could block my swing.

06:55.740 --> 06:58.640
Your skills have improved, Your Majesty.

06:59.980 --> 07:01.890
My right hand feels weak.

07:02.720 --> 07:05.150
Did that single blow sprain it?

07:05.430 --> 07:06.960
Good.

07:07.780 --> 07:10.530
You're a commander worth killing.

07:24.020 --> 07:30.710
I wish we had time to play,
but I'm in a hurry.

07:31.190 --> 07:35.220
Your head is mine.

07:49.630 --> 07:53.490
Bastard! How dare you kick the king!

08:01.120 --> 08:06.280
Die!

08:19.260 --> 08:21.660
Your Majesty, give your sword to me.

08:21.660 --> 08:22.930
Please stand back.

08:23.580 --> 08:26.150
Damn it.

08:30.350 --> 08:32.340
King's guard, fall back!

08:32.340 --> 08:34.490
Defend the king!

08:38.240 --> 08:41.280
Damn it!

08:41.280 --> 08:43.450
Stop, Thorgil!

08:44.560 --> 08:46.810
Don't pursue him too far, Wulf.

08:46.810 --> 08:48.710
You're seriously injured as well.

08:49.890 --> 08:55.840
I let my guard down,
but more than that, he's a bold man.

08:57.150 --> 08:59.400
I wish he'd serve me again.

09:01.180 --> 09:03.930
King's guard, fall back!

09:04.300 --> 09:06.980
His Majesty is under attack!

09:06.980 --> 09:09.060
All forces, fall back!

09:09.060 --> 09:12.260
Run! Hurry!

09:14.220 --> 09:15.440
Your Majesty!

09:15.440 --> 09:16.980
Your Majesty!

09:15.980 --> 09:17.640
Wh-What's going on?

09:18.370 --> 09:22.200
Who would do something like that?
Was it Thorgil?

09:26.620 --> 09:27.960
That was close.

09:32.670 --> 09:35.050
Master, are you alive?

09:39.230 --> 09:40.300
Okay.

09:40.980 --> 09:46.350
Looks like those soldiers
didn't recognize you.

09:46.350 --> 09:48.310
You're a lucky man.

09:49.740 --> 09:51.810
Damn heavy, too.

09:54.540 --> 09:58.320
Don't think you can get off easy by dying.

09:59.200 --> 10:06.390
You have responsibilities as the
losing force's leader, Iron Fist Ketil.

10:23.540 --> 10:25.830
I hear it...

10:30.700 --> 10:36.880
The sound I heard when my village burned.

10:39.380 --> 10:42.920
The sound of the world falling apart.

10:46.100 --> 10:49.960
They're fighting, aren't they?

10:51.520 --> 10:54.500
It's all right. Don't worry.

10:55.360 --> 10:57.410
We aren't slaves anymore.

10:58.060 --> 11:00.040
We're leaving this farm.

11:01.410 --> 11:06.120
That battle has nothing to do with us.

11:11.200 --> 11:16.060
Where will we go once we leave this place?

11:20.050 --> 11:21.940
We can go to my village.

11:23.470 --> 11:26.740
It's a bit cold, but it's a nice place.

11:30.480 --> 11:34.820
Do you have slaves there?

11:36.620 --> 11:41.060
Do you have wars?

11:43.900 --> 11:48.230
Yes. Battles were fought there once.

11:48.770 --> 11:52.850
I'd be lying if I said
it would never happen again.

11:56.830 --> 12:00.240
I'm not going.

12:01.580 --> 12:06.360
I'm going somewhere else.

12:08.830 --> 12:12.820
Gardar and the children...

12:16.670 --> 12:19.780
are waiting for me.

12:22.190 --> 12:26.100
I just wanted to express my gratitude.

12:31.010 --> 12:36.760
Thank you, Einar and Thorfinn.

12:38.660 --> 12:40.640
Thank you.

12:46.080 --> 12:56.080
I felt like I was wandering through
a terrible nightmare all alone.

13:00.140 --> 13:01.570
But...

13:09.970 --> 13:13.430
Our morning chats...

13:16.000 --> 13:21.350
I enjoyed your stories, Einar...

13:24.320 --> 13:26.190
No, Arnheid!

13:26.820 --> 13:29.720
Hang in there, Arnheid!

13:30.750 --> 13:32.440
Arnheid!

13:33.950 --> 13:39.790
Didn't you say you'd protect
the child inside you?

13:40.150 --> 13:42.180
Arnheid!

13:48.060 --> 13:52.300
The child has already gone
to the other side.

13:59.650 --> 14:01.720
They're all dead.

14:03.490 --> 14:06.310
All of my loved ones.

14:07.900 --> 14:12.360
What point is there in going on living?

14:15.180 --> 14:19.760
There's nothing left for me here.

14:22.550 --> 14:26.390
Why do I have to live?

14:31.120 --> 14:38.220
I... Because... Because I...

14:43.170 --> 14:45.900
Arnheid? Arnheid?

14:46.590 --> 14:47.900
Arnheid!

14:47.900 --> 14:49.840
Move, Einar!

14:54.450 --> 14:59.920
My father taught me this technique to
bring someone back from the dead.

15:00.860 --> 15:04.290
Einar, speak to her as loudly as you can.

15:06.320 --> 15:09.170
Arnheid, don't go!

15:09.540 --> 15:16.300
I... I love you! I need you!

15:16.930 --> 15:19.930
I want you to laugh at my stories again!

15:19.930 --> 15:22.230
Please live!

15:23.480 --> 15:25.540
Live with me again!

15:26.940 --> 15:30.480
Please live!

15:43.680 --> 15:46.330
Einar, that's enough.

16:46.500 --> 16:48.260
Far to the west...

16:51.890 --> 16:59.140
and across the sea,
there's a place called Vinland.

17:01.390 --> 17:04.800
Warm and bountiful, it is a distant land,

17:05.630 --> 17:11.430
beyond the reach of slave-traders
and the flames of war.

17:12.770 --> 17:18.600
You would be able to live
without suffering there.

17:21.420 --> 17:22.740
Arnheid...

17:24.690 --> 17:28.120
Let's go there together.

17:29.250 --> 17:33.280
Let's build a peaceful nation in Vinland.

17:57.630 --> 18:02.260
It's you guys. What are you still doing here?

18:11.280 --> 18:12.770
Don't, Einar!

18:13.630 --> 18:15.020
Ketil!

18:16.620 --> 18:19.600
You! You killed Arnheid!

18:21.210 --> 18:24.720
I'll kill you. I'll fucking kill you!

18:26.660 --> 18:30.960
Don't, Einar! Killing the master
won't help anything!

18:36.580 --> 18:39.590
I see. Arnheid is dead.

18:41.490 --> 18:43.340
Open your eyes, Einar!

18:43.800 --> 18:44.970
Please!

18:45.460 --> 18:46.720
Einar!

19:15.780 --> 19:23.270
Einar, killing the master
won't quell your rage.

19:25.410 --> 19:27.400
Anger begets more anger.

19:28.560 --> 19:30.820
It just results in deaths, one after another.

19:32.360 --> 19:37.610
I was stuck in that hell for a long time.

19:39.860 --> 19:42.680
Please, Einar.

19:43.500 --> 19:47.520
Don't fall under the same curse
that afflicted me.

20:23.230 --> 20:24.210
Dad...

20:24.910 --> 20:28.360
I know. Get the ship ready to depart.

21:00.770 --> 21:07.250
God... must be watching us,
even as we stand here now.

21:14.430 --> 21:18.660
People losing friends, and parents
and children killing each other...

21:19.470 --> 21:25.510
He must be looking down on everything
from up high in heaven.

21:40.850 --> 21:41.920
Thorfinn...

21:42.810 --> 21:45.320
Wait. Where are you going?

21:45.740 --> 21:48.320
Wait! What do you intend to do?

21:49.820 --> 21:52.320
I'm going to see Canute.

21:52.730 --> 21:53.430
What?

21:54.880 --> 21:58.470
The master is still alive.
He hasn't been captured.

21:59.030 --> 22:01.080
The battle isn't over.

22:02.450 --> 22:05.800
I may be able to prevent more deaths.

22:06.540 --> 22:09.490
That's ridiculous. We need to
leave this place immediately.

22:10.360 --> 22:13.970
Why do you have to do this?

22:15.720 --> 22:16.470
Thorfinn!

22:24.540 --> 22:26.260
This time...

22:26.260 --> 22:31.190
This time, please let me
take you back to Iceland.

22:32.990 --> 22:34.020
Please.

22:39.650 --> 22:43.960
Long ago, you once told me...

22:46.140 --> 22:55.720
that our ancestors fled from war
and ended up in Iceland.

22:58.140 --> 23:03.910
At the time, I thought it was lame,

23:05.200 --> 23:09.190
but now, I'm really proud of them.

23:10.270 --> 23:11.410
Thorfinn...

23:14.980 --> 23:20.020
I'd estimate Canute
only brought around 100 men.

23:21.280 --> 23:23.430
No matter how badly it turns out,

23:25.310 --> 23:28.710
I should be able to make it back alive.

23:40.240 --> 23:44.690
We'll have the ship
ready to depart at any time.

23:45.380 --> 23:46.640
Don't push yourself too hard!

23:47.820 --> 23:53.660
We're going back to Iceland,
no matter what, Thorfinn!

25:36.260 --> 25:39.970
Courage

25:37.870 --> 25:39.170
"Courage."
